<header><p class="enc-kicker">State</p><h1 class="enc-title">Gupta Empire</h1><p class="enc-meta">Also known as Guptas, Gupta dynasty, Gupta</p></header>
<div class="enc-body"><p class="enc-desc">The Gupta Empire was a major state of northern <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/india">India</a> from the fourth to the sixth century CE, often regarded as a classical age of Indian culture. It is associated with achievements in <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/sanskrit">Sanskrit</a> literature, mathematics, astronomy and art. It has its own profile on the site and is also discussed as a later successor in the region once ruled by the <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/maurya-empire">Maurya Empire</a>.</p><figure class="enc-fig"><img src="/images/encyclopedia/gupta-empire.jpg" alt="Gupta Empire" width="320" height="296" fetchpriority="high"><figcaption>Image: Map created from DEMIS Mapserver, which are public domain. Koba-chan. · CC BY-SA 3.0 · <a href="https://commons.wikimedia.org/wiki/File:Map_of_the_Gupta_Empire.png" target="_blank" rel="noopener">Wikimedia Commons</a></figcaption></figure></div>
